                {
                  "type": "frame",
                  "id": "i0r71",
                  "name": "The Experience",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "layout": "vertical",
                  "gap": 20,
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "id": "Wu0Fc",
                      "name": "bexpTitle",
                      "fill": "$--color-primary",
                      "content": "The Experience",
                      "fontFamily": "Playfair Display",
                      "fontSize": 28,
                      "fontWeight": "600"
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "id": "9h29x",
                      "name": "bexpBody",
                      "fill": "$--color-text",
                      "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                      "width": "fill_container",
                      "content": "Discover the enchanting heart of Stockholm on this intimate walking tour through Gamla Stan, the city's beautifully preserved medieval old town. Your certified guide will bring centuries of history to life as you wander through narrow cobblestone streets, past colorful merchant houses, and into hidden courtyards that most visitors never find.\n\nFrom the grandeur of the Royal Palace to the charm of Stortorget — Scandinavia's oldest square — every corner tells a story. Learn about Viking origins, medieval trade routes, the Stockholm Bloodbath, and the Nobel Prize legacy.\n\nYour journey begins at the iconic Kungliga Slottet (Royal Palace), where you'll hear tales of royal intrigue spanning five centuries. As you descend into the labyrinth of Gamla Stan's narrow alleys, your guide will reveal the hidden stories behind the colorful facades — from the cannonball embedded in a wall on Österlånggatan to the tiny iron boy statue tucked away in a forgotten courtyard.\n\nThe tour continues through Stortorget, the oldest public square in Stockholm, where the infamous Stockholm Bloodbath of 1520 forever changed Scandinavian history. Here, your guide will paint a vivid picture of the dramatic events that led to the birth of modern Sweden.\n\nAlong the way, you'll discover the Nobel Museum, the German Church with its magnificent baroque interior, and Mårten Trotzigs Gränd — the narrowest alley in Stockholm at just 90 centimeters wide. Every step reveals another layer of this remarkable city's 700-year story.\n\nThe experience concludes with a visit to Riddarholmen, the peaceful island adjacent to Gamla Stan, where medieval churches and waterfront views provide the perfect ending to your journey through time.",
                      "lineHeight": 1.7,
                      "fontFamily": "Inter",
                      "fontSize": 16,
                      "fontWeight": "normal"
                    }
                  ]
                },
